-- #1618 — the PERMUTATION pair for the effect-carrying head, Int-rowed impl
-- declared FIRST. Partner: effect_head_impl_ba.mdk.
--
-- Expected `(2, 3)`, hand-derived: the rows are transparent, so these are impls
-- at heads `Int` and `Bool` respectively — two distinct heads, no overlap, and
-- `sz 0` / `sz True` each match exactly one. Declaration order cannot matter.
--
-- Why a pair at all when the filed repro has one impl: peeling the row moves
-- these impls out of the shared headless bucket into two SEPARATE per-head
-- buckets. A single-impl fixture cannot distinguish "peeled to the right head"
-- from "peeled to any head at all", because with one candidate every bucket
-- answers the same. Two impls that must land in DIFFERENT buckets can.
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int

impl Sz (<Stdout> Int) where
  sz _ = 2

impl Sz (<Stdout> Bool) where
  sz _ = 3

main = println (sz 0, sz True)
